IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `sa-interpretation-time`
IMPORT `sa-part4-repeal-and-amendment`
IMPORT `sa-part7-references-distance-amounts`
IMPORT `sa-part8-documents`
IMPORT `sa-part9-penalties-and-proceedings`
IMPORT `sa-part9-standard-scales`

-- Legislation Interpretation Act 2021 (South Australia), version 20.11.2025 -- THE SEAT LAYER.
--
-- SEAT: a person who has a time limit to meet under a South Australian Act or statutory instrument
-- (to apply, object, appeal, reply or pay), or who needs to know when something takes effect, asking
-- on which day their period ends and which of their days count.
--
-- This layer phrases the rules already encoded in the modules imported above as the questions that
-- person asks. Nothing here is new law, and no rule is restated: each question builds the records
-- the modules expect from plain answers and then calls the module rule.
--
-- Provisions that address only an official (the performance of functions, powers of appointment and
-- delegation, gender balance in nominations, the rules of reading that bind a court) are encoded in
-- the layer-1 modules for what they decide and have no question here.
--
-- Plain inputs. Every question takes plain inputs: yes or no, a number, a date, or a choice from a
-- list the modules define. A day is asked as a date. A time within a day is asked as a number of hours
-- (0 is the start of the day, 24 the stroke of midnight that ends it).
-- Public holidays are asked as one run of consecutive days (its first day and how many days it has), because
-- the Public Holidays Act 2023 is not among the sources. A weekend day inside the run is harmless: it is
-- not a business day anyway. A public holiday that lasts only part of a day does not make a day a non-business
-- day (s 46), so such a day is left out of the run; the module field for it is a fixed placeholder.
--
-- A period of weeks, a period that begins "from a specified day", the second anniversary of a 29 February and
-- the like are answered by the modules with NOTHING (the text does not say); those questions return a MAYBE
-- and NOTHING means "the Act does not answer this".

§ `Legislation Interpretation Act 2021 (SA) -- the questions of a person with a time limit`

DECLARE `Unit my period is counted in` IS ONE OF
    days
    weeks
    months
    years

§§ `When an Act or a provision takes effect or ends`

-- ss 27(1), 27(2). "Assent" is the Governor's, or the Crown's, agreement that makes a Bill an Act.
@export On which day does my Act come into operation if it fixes no day for its commencement (s 27(1), (2))?
GIVEN `my Bill was reserved for the signification of Her Majesty's assent` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the Bill for your Act reserved for the signification of Her Majesty's assent?
      `the day assent was given` IS A DATE @desc On what day was the Bill assented to?
      `the day assent was notified by proclamation` IS A DATE @desc If the Bill was reserved, on what day was the assent notified by proclamation in the State? (If it was not reserved, give the same day as above.)
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `On which day does my Act come into operation` IS
    `s 27(1): the day an Act with no commencement provision comes into operation`
        (`s 27(2): the day a Bill is taken to have been assented to` `my Bill was reserved for the signification of Her Majesty's assent` `the day assent was given` `the day assent was notified by proclamation`)

-- ss 27(3), 27(5). A proclamation is the Governor's notice fixing a day for a provision to start.
-- A later proclamation made before the day an earlier one fixed takes its place.
@export On which day does a proclamation bring my provision into operation (s 27(3), (5))?
GIVEN `the first proclamation was made on` IS A DATE @desc On what day was the first proclamation made?
      `the first proclamation fixes` IS A DATE @desc What day does the first proclamation fix for the provision to come into operation?
      `a second proclamation was made` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was a second proclamation made?
      `the second proclamation was made on` IS A DATE @desc If so, on what day was it made? (Any day if there was none.)
      `the second proclamation fixes` IS A DATE @desc If so, what day does it fix? (Any day if there was none.)
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
DECIDE `On which day does a proclamation bring my provision into operation` IS
    `s 27(3) and (5): the day fixed by the proclamations made so far` `my proclamations`
    WHERE
        `my proclamations` MEANS
            IF `a second proclamation was made`
            THEN LIST (Proclamation OF `the first proclamation was made on`, (JUST `the first proclamation fixes`)), (Proclamation OF `the second proclamation was made on`, (JUST `the second proclamation fixes`))
            ELSE LIST (Proclamation OF `the first proclamation was made on`, (JUST `the first proclamation fixes`))

-- ss 27(6), 27(7). An Act or provision to be brought in by proclamation that has not been brought in comes into operation on the
-- second anniversary of assent, unless the Act or provision says this does not apply.
@export On which day does my provision come into operation if no proclamation has brought it in sooner (s 27(6), (7))?
GIVEN `section 27(6) covers my Act or provision` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your Act or provision one to be brought into operation by proclamation, as section 27(6) describes?
      `my Act or provision says section 27(6) does not apply` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does your Act or provision say that section 27(6) does not apply to it?
      `the day my Act was assented to` IS A DATE @desc On what day was your Act assented to?
      `a proclamation has brought it in` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has a proclamation brought your provision into operation?
      `the day the proclamation brought it in` IS A DATE @desc If so, on what day? (Any day if none.)
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
DECIDE `On which day does my provision come into operation if no proclamation has brought it in sooner` IS
    `s 27(6) and (7): the day an Act or provision to be brought into operation by proclamation comes into operation`
        `section 27(6) covers my Act or provision` `my Act or provision says section 27(6) does not apply` `the day my Act was assented to` `my proclaimed day`
    WHERE
        `my proclaimed day` MEANS IF `a proclamation has brought it in` THEN JUST `the day the proclamation brought it in` ELSE NOTHING

-- ss 28, 30. A provision that comes into operation on a day does so at the beginning of that day, and one that expires on a
-- day continues to have effect until the end of that day.
@export Is my Act or provision in operation at the time I ask about (ss 28, 30)?
GIVEN `the day it comes into operation` IS A DATE @desc On what day does it come into operation?
      `it is expressed to expire on a day` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it say it expires, lapses or ceases to have effect on a day, or that it continues in force until a day?
      `the day it expires` IS A DATE @desc If so, on what day? (Any day if it does not say.)
      `the day I ask about` IS A DATE @desc On what day do you want to know?
      `hours into that day` IS A NUMBER @desc At what time on that day? Give hours since the day began (0 is the start of the day, 24 is the stroke of midnight that ends it).
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my Act or provision in operation at the time I ask about` IF
    `ss 28 and 30: a provision is in operation at a moment` `the moment it comes into operation` `its expiry day` `the moment I ask about`
    WHERE
        `the moment it comes into operation` MEANS `s 28: the moment an Act or provision comes into operation on a particular day` `the day it comes into operation`
        `its expiry day` MEANS IF `it is expressed to expire on a day` THEN JUST `the day it expires` ELSE NOTHING
        `the moment I ask about` MEANS Moment WITH `calendar day` IS `the day I ask about`, `seconds into the day` IS `hours into that day` TIMES 3600

-- s 32(2). The repeal, amendment or expiry of an Act does not revive what was not in force, and does not affect what was done under it,
-- the rights, duties and penalties created or incurred under it, or proceedings in respect of them.
@export Does the repeal, amendment or expiry affect what I have under the Act (s 32(2))?
GIVEN `my Act, instrument or provision has been repealed or amended, or has expired` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Act, instrument or provision been repealed or amended, or has it expired?
      `what I ask about` IS A `Thing a repeal, amendment or expiry might touch` @desc What do you want to know about?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does the repeal, amendment or expiry affect what I have under the Act` IS
    `the repeal, amendment or expiry affects` `my Act, instrument or provision has been repealed or amended, or has expired` `what I ask about`

§§ `Counting my period`

-- s 44(1), with the units of s 4. A "business day" is a day that is not a Saturday, a Sunday or a public holiday.
@export On which day does my period end (s 4 "day", "month", "year"; s 44(1))?
GIVEN `how my period begins` IS A `How a period is expressed to begin` @desc How does the law say your period begins: at, on or with a specified day; on, from or after the happening of an act or event; after a specified day; or from a specified day?
      `the day it begins by` IS A DATE @desc What is the specified day, or the day the act or event happened?
      `the unit of my period` IS A `Unit my period is counted in` @desc Is the period counted in days, weeks, months or years?
      `how long my period is` IS A NUMBER @desc How many of those units is the period?
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
DECIDE `On which day does my period end` IS
    `s 44(1): the last day of a period` `how my period begins` `the day it begins by` `my period's length`
    WHERE
        `my period's length` MEANS
            CONSIDER `the unit of my period`
                WHEN days THEN `a number of days` `how long my period is`
                WHEN weeks THEN `a number of weeks` `how long my period is`
                WHEN months THEN `a number of months` `how long my period is`
                WHEN years THEN `a number of years` `how long my period is`

-- s 44(2). If the last day for doing a thing is not a business day, the thing may be done on the next day that is.
@export On which day is the last I may do the thing, if the last day of my period is not a business day (s 44(2))?
GIVEN `how my period begins` IS A `How a period is expressed to begin` @desc How does the law say your period begins: at, on or with a specified day; on, from or after the happening of an act or event; after a specified day; or from a specified day?
      `the day it begins by` IS A DATE @desc What is the specified day, or the day the act or event happened?
      `the unit of my period` IS A `Unit my period is counted in` @desc Is the period counted in days, weeks, months or years?
      `how long my period is` IS A NUMBER @desc How many of those units is the period?
      `a run of public holidays begins on` IS A DATE @desc If a run of consecutive public holidays falls near the end of your period, on what day does it begin? (Any day if none.)
      `the run has this many days` IS A NUMBER @desc How many days are in that run? (0 if there are none.)
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
DECIDE `On which day is the last I may do the thing` IS
    `s 44(1) and (2): the last day on which a thing may be done within a period` `how my period begins` `the day it begins by` `my period's length` `my public holidays`
    WHERE
        `my period's length` MEANS
            CONSIDER `the unit of my period`
                WHEN days THEN `a number of days` `how long my period is`
                WHEN weeks THEN `a number of weeks` `how long my period is`
                WHEN months THEN `a number of months` `how long my period is`
                WHEN years THEN `a number of years` `how long my period is`
        `my public holidays` MEANS `the public holidays in a run` `a run of public holidays begins on` `the run has this many days`

-- Builds the list of public holidays from a run of consecutive days. This is the seat's way of asking for the list; it is not a rule.
-- Each day is a full-day public holiday: the field for a part-day holiday is a fixed placeholder, FALSE (see the heading of this file).
GIVEN `the first day of the run` IS A DATE, `the number of days in the run` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A LIST OF `Public holiday`
`the public holidays in a run` MEANS
    IF `the number of days in the run` AT MOST 0
    THEN EMPTY
    ELSE (`Public holiday` OF (`the first day of the run` PLUS (`the number of days in the run` MINUS 1)), FALSE) FOLLOWED BY `the public holidays in a run` `the first day of the run` (`the number of days in the run` MINUS 1)

@export Is the day I ask about a business day (s 4 "business day"; s 46)?
GIVEN `the day I ask about` IS A DATE @desc Which day do you want to know about?
      `a run of public holidays begins on` IS A DATE @desc If a run of consecutive public holidays includes that day or falls near it, on what day does the run begin? (Any day if none.)
      `the run has this many days` IS A NUMBER @desc How many days are in that run? (0 if there are none.)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is the day I ask about a business day` IF
    `s 4: is a business day` `the day I ask about` (`the public holidays in a run` `a run of public holidays begins on` `the run has this many days`)

-- s 44(1) items 4, 5 and 7.
@export On which day does my period end, if it runs up to a day the law names (s 44(1), items 4, 5 and 7)?
GIVEN `how my period ends` IS A `How a period is expressed to end` @desc Does the law say the period continues until a specified day; ends at, on or with a specified day; or ends before a specified day?
      `the specified day` IS A DATE @desc What is the specified day?
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `On which day does my period end if it runs up to a day the law names` IS
    `s 44(1) items 4, 5 and 7: the last day of a period that ends by reference to a specified day` `how my period ends` `the specified day`

-- s 44(1) item 1.
@export Is the day I ask about one of the days of a period expressed to occur between two days (s 44(1), item 1)?
GIVEN `the earlier day` IS A DATE @desc What is the earlier of the two days the period is expressed to occur between?
      `the later day` IS A DATE @desc What is the later of the two days?
      `the day I ask about` IS A DATE @desc Which day do you want to know about?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is the day I ask about one of the days of a period between two days` IS
    `s 44(1) item 1: a day is one of the days of a period expressed to occur between 2 days` `the earlier day` `the later day` `the day I ask about`

-- s 44(3).
@export Must I do the thing as soon as is reasonably practicable (s 44(3))?
GIVEN `I am required to do the thing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does an Act or instrument require you to do the thing?
      `a period is provided or allowed for doing it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the Act or instrument provide or allow a period of time for doing it?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must I do the thing as soon as is reasonably practicable` IS
    `s 44(3): the thing must be done as soon as is reasonably practicable` `I am required to do the thing` `a period is provided or allowed for doing it`

-- s 49. A person attains a particular age at the beginning of the anniversary of their birth; for a 29 February birth,
-- at the beginning of 1 March in a year that is not a leap year.
@export On which day do I attain a particular age (s 49)?
GIVEN `my date of birth` IS A DATE @desc What is your date of birth?
      `the age in years` IS A NUMBER @desc What age, in years, do you want to know about?
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `On which day do I attain a particular age` IS
    (`s 49: the moment a person attains an age in years` `my date of birth` `the age in years`)'s `calendar day`

-- s 50. An amount calculated for a tax, fee, charge or other amount that is not an exact multiple of 5 cents is rounded down.
@export What amount must I pay after the amount is rounded down to a multiple of 5 cents (s 50)?
GIVEN `the Act or instrument provides for the calculation and payment of the amount` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does an Act or instrument provide for the calculation and payment of the tax, fee, charge or other amount?
      `the calculated amount in cents` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the amount as calculated, in cents? (For $23.07, give 2307.)
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `What amount must I pay after the amount is rounded down to a multiple of 5 cents` IS
    `the amount payable after rounding down to a multiple of 5 cents` `the Act or instrument provides for the calculation and payment of the amount` `the calculated amount in cents`

§§ `Having a document served on me, or serving one`

-- s 51(2). Asked from the position of the person to be served, an individual.
@export May a document be served on me, an individual, in this way (s 51(2))?
GIVEN `the way it is served` IS A `Way of serving a document on an individual` @desc How was, or would, the document be served?
      `I have designated a physical address` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you designated a physical address for the service of documents of that kind?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May a document be served on me, an individual, in this way` IS
    `the document may be served on an individual in this way` `the way it is served` `I have designated a physical address`

-- s 51(3). Asked from the position of the person to be served, a body corporate.
@export May a document be served on my body corporate in this way (s 51(3))?
GIVEN `the way it is served` IS A `Way of serving a document on a body corporate` @desc How was, or would, the document be served?
      `we have designated a physical address` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the body corporate designated a physical address for the service of documents of that kind?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May a document be served on my body corporate in this way` IS
    `the document may be served on a body corporate in this way` `the way it is served` `we have designated a physical address`

-- s 51(4).
@export Was my document posted to the address (s 51(4))?
GIVEN `I properly addressed it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you properly address the document?
      `I prepaid it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you prepay the postage?
      `I posted it as a letter` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you post it as a letter?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Was my document posted to the address` IS
    `a document is posted to an address` `I properly addressed it` `I prepaid it` `I posted it as a letter`

-- s 51(5). Unless the contrary is proved, service by post is taken to be effected when the document would be delivered
-- in the ordinary course of post.
@export On which day is a document I posted taken to have been served (s 51(5))?
GIVEN `the day it would be delivered in the ordinary course of post` IS A DATE @desc On what day would the document be delivered in the ordinary course of post for the postal service used?
      `the contrary is proved` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has it been proved that the document was served at some other time?
      `the day it is proved it was served` IS A DATE @desc If so, on what day? (Any day if not.)
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
DECIDE `On which day is a document I posted taken to have been served` IS
    CONSIDER `s 51(5): the moment service by post is taken to be effected` `the moment of ordinary delivery` `the contrary is proved` `the moment proved, if the contrary is proved`
        WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
        WHEN JUST `the moment` THEN JUST (`the moment`'s `calendar day`)
    WHERE
        -- Placeholder: only the day of the moment is returned, so the seconds fields are fixed at the start of the day.
        `the moment of ordinary delivery` MEANS `s 4: the beginning of a day` `the day it would be delivered in the ordinary course of post`
        `the moment proved, if the contrary is proved` MEANS IF `the contrary is proved` THEN JUST (`s 4: the beginning of a day` `the day it is proved it was served`) ELSE NOTHING

-- s 52.
@export Is the form I used sufficient (s 52)?
GIVEN `a form is prescribed or approved` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is a form prescribed or approved by or for the purposes of the Act or instrument?
      `my form is to the same effect` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the form you used to the same effect?
      `my deviations are calculated to mislead` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the differences between your form and the prescribed or approved form calculated to mislead?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is the form I used sufficient` IS
    `the form used is sufficient` `a form is prescribed or approved` `my form is to the same effect` `my deviations are calculated to mislead`

§§ `Penalties and fees`

-- s 53(2). Asked about an offence the person is charged with, a penalty that has changed.
@export Does a changed penalty apply to my offence (s 53(2))?
GIVEN `the change` IS A `Change to the penalty for an offence` @desc Was the penalty for the offence increased or reduced?
      `the day I committed the offence` IS A DATE @desc On what day was the offence committed?
      `hours into that day I committed it` IS A NUMBER @desc At what time? Give hours since the day began (0 is the start of the day, 24 is midnight at its end).
      `the day the change takes effect` IS A DATE @desc On what day does the change to the penalty take effect?
      `the day the penalty is imposed` IS A DATE @desc On what day is the penalty imposed?
      `hours into that day it is imposed` IS A NUMBER @desc At what time? Give hours since the day began.
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does a changed penalty apply to my offence` IS
    `the changed penalty applies to the offence` `the change` `the moment I committed it` `the moment the change takes effect` `the moment it is imposed`
    WHERE
        `the moment I committed it` MEANS Moment WITH `calendar day` IS `the day I committed the offence`, `seconds into the day` IS `hours into that day I committed it` TIMES 3600
        -- Section 28: a change takes effect at the beginning of its day.
        `the moment the change takes effect` MEANS `s 4: the beginning of a day` `the day the change takes effect`
        `the moment it is imposed` MEANS Moment WITH `calendar day` IS `the day the penalty is imposed`, `seconds into the day` IS `hours into that day it is imposed` TIMES 3600

-- s 54. Imprisonment is answered in months; a fine or an expiation fee in dollars.
@export What is the standard penalty or fee for a division (s 54)?
GIVEN `the division` IS A NUMBER @desc Which division of the standard scale (1 to 12)?
      `the kind of entry` IS A `Kind of scale entry` @desc Is it the imprisonment, the fine or the expiation fee?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `What is the standard penalty or fee for a division` IS
    `the amount the table in section 54 gives` `the division` `the kind of entry`
